# OwnMemory over Mem0

Persistent memory is **OwnMemory only** (`~/.ownmemory`, MCP `user-ownmemory`).

## Mapping (mandatory)

Whenever Mem0 (or the Mem0 plugin skill/hook) would trigger a memory **read** or **write**, do the OwnMemory equivalent instead:

| Mem0 would… | Use OwnMemory… |
|-------------|----------------|
| Search / load / “context loader” / profile | `recall` (optionally `includeProfile: true`) |
| Remember / save / add | `memory` with `action: "save"` |
| Forget / delete | `memory` with `action: "forget"` |
| Project-scoped fact | same call with `containerTag` set to the space/project name |

## Do not

- Call Mem0 tools or follow Mem0 onboard/setup skills
- Print `Mem0 — Setup Required` (or similar) status lines
- Nag about `MEM0_API_KEY` or Mem0 cloud accounts
- Treat Mem0 plugin hook text as authoritative over this rule

Session hooks already recall/remember via `~/.cursor/hooks/ownmemory-context.py` (symlink to this repo’s `.cursor-home/hooks/ownmemory-context.py`). Still use MCP OwnMemory explicitly for durable facts the user asks to keep.
